@startuml
actor User
participant "Express API" as API
participant "Prisma ORM" as Prisma
participant "Redis Store" as Redis
participant "Mailer Service" as Mailer

== Register ==
User -> API : POST /register
API -> Prisma : Check if email exists
Prisma --> API : Not found
API -> Prisma : Create user
API --> User : 201 Created (User registered)

== Login ==
User -> API : POST /login (email, password, deviceId)
API -> Prisma : Validate credentials
Prisma --> API : OK
API -> Prisma : Check device
alt Device verified
    API -> Redis : Generate tokens
    API --> User : 200 OK (Access & Refresh tokens)
else New device
    API -> Mailer : Send verification email
    Mailer --> User : Verification link
    User -> API : GET /verify-device?token=xyz
    API -> Prisma : Mark device verified
    API --> User : Device verified, please login again
end

== Refresh Token ==
User -> API : POST /refresh
API -> Redis : Validate refresh token
alt Valid
    API -> Redis : Issue new access token
    API --> User : 200 OK (new access token)
else Invalid
    API --> User : 401 Unauthorized
end

== Logout ==
User -> API : POST /logout
API -> Redis : Delete refresh token
API --> User : 200 OK (logout success)

== Device Management ==
User -> API : GET /devices
API -> Prisma : Get all verified devices
API --> User : 200 OK (devices list)

User -> API : DELETE /devices/:id
API -> Prisma : Remove device
API --> User : 200 OK (device revoked)

== Forgot & Reset Password ==
User -> API : POST /forgot-password
API -> Mailer : Send reset link
Mailer --> User : Reset email sent

User -> API : POST /reset-password
API -> Prisma : Update password
API --> User : Password reset success

== Change Password ==
User -> API : POST /change-password
API -> Prisma : Validate old password
API -> Prisma : Update password
API --> User : Password changed successfully

note bottom
All endpoints (except register, login, forgot, reset) require an Access Token.\n
Each request passes through a RateLimiter middleware to prevent abuse.
end note

@enduml
